Files in page_scripts/:
- linkedin_section_content.js: linkedin_mcp_server/linkedin/content.py (PageContentReader._extract_root_content)

Python ports:
- linkedin/links.py: linkedin_mcp_server/linkedin/link_metadata.py
- linkedin/sections.py: linkedin_mcp_server/linkedin/capture.py, linkedin/content.py, linkedin/text.py, core/utils.py
  (section capture, "Show more" expansion, popup close, overlay read, page chrome markers and player-control lines)
- linkedin/profile.py: linkedin_mcp_server/linkedin/fields.py, linkedin/person.py (profile section pages)
- linkedin/company.py: linkedin_mcp_server/linkedin/fields.py, linkedin/company.py (company section pages)
- linkedin/posts.py: linkedin_mcp_server/linkedin/posts.py, linkedin/search_urls.py (post search URL and filters)

Changes made by Tool Store:
- Only the page-reading logic is ported; the single-user browser, process and installer code is not used.
- Pages run in our per-user browser sessions (browser_session.SitePage); scrolling uses OpenCLI's auto_scroll.js.
- linkedin/sections.py adds LinkedIn upsell lines (Premium, Sales Navigator, "Key signals") and the
  "People who follow X also follow" box seen on live pages, and lets a section end at its own markers
  (profile main page before its activity feed, company About page before recruiting and locations).
- linkedin/links.py drops people, companies, schools and outside links whose label (or, unlabelled, address)
  is not in the section's text ("People also viewed" suggestions, cut-off parts), ignores number-only labels, counts /posts/ links as posts, and leaves out messaging and
  company-id search links.
- linkedin/posts.py does not port the response listener that collects extra post links.
